From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: avdim <avdimdv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:08:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arizona: Drop the Wolfson Control regmap hook

arizona-control ("Wolfson Control", /sys/class/misc/wolfson_control) hooks
every regmap write via _regmap_write(). The hook drops map->lock in the
middle of the write, so read-modify-write sequences are no longer
atomic. DAPM, the arizona IRQ thread and mixer writes can then lose each
other's bits. Its callbacks also issue nested codec writes from inside
the hook, guarded only by an unprotected global ignore_next flag.

It also silently replaces "hidden" fields with the value first written
at boot. SPKOUT (OUT4) mix input 1 is locked to AIF1RX1/2: mixer and
tinymix writes report success but never reach the chip, while DAPM
believes them. Routing DRC1 or EQ3 to the speaker therefore left DAPM
managing a path that did not exist in hardware. Its own speaker-EQ
bridge stalls speaker playback (out_write I/O error) until the codec is
reset.

Remove the hook call and do not register the sysfs interface. Without
the hook, sysfs writes would only bypass DAPM. Codec register writes now
behave as upstream, and mixer_paths/DAPM fully own the routing. The
cost is that apps driving wolfson_control (Deathly Adiutor sound
controls) stop working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I54759e9a9a8edbcabbda0365a3426d2edd52da99
---
 drivers/base/regmap/regmap.c | 6 ------
 sound/soc/codecs/wm5102.c    | 4 ----
 2 files changed, 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/regmap/regmap.c b/drivers/base/regmap/regmap.c
index 8dd07f49..8850f581 100644
--- a/drivers/base/regmap/regmap.c
+++ b/drivers/base/regmap/regmap.c
@@ -485,12 +485,6 @@ int _regmap_write(struct regmap *map, unsigned int reg,
 	int ret;
 	BUG_ON(!map->format.format_write && !map->format.format_val);
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_MFD_ARIZONA
-	mutex_unlock(&map->lock);
-	arizona_control_regmap_hook(map, reg, &val);
-	mutex_lock(&map->lock);
-#endif
-
 	if (!map->cache_bypass && map->format.format_write) {
 		ret = regcache_write(map, reg, val);
 		if (ret != 0)
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wm5102.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wm5102.c
index 2410c94d..f4489ca2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wm5102.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wm5102.c
@@ -1681,10 +1681,6 @@ static int wm5102_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_codec *codec)
 
 	priv->core.arizona->dapm = &codec->dapm;
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_MFD_ARIZONA
-	arizona_control_init(codec);
-#endif
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
